From: ADP Monitor Windows engine build <276656355+alexfused@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] loader: Use the engine's own bundle identifier on macOS.

The macOS loader embeds an Info.plist (__TEXT,__info_plist), and macOS
names a process started from it by that plist's CFBundleIdentifier. Use
the engine's own App ID, com.alexparkin.adpmonitor.winehost, which is
also the loader's code-signing identifier: the engine is then neither
WineHQ's org.winehq.wine signed by someone else nor ADP Monitor
(com.alexparkin.adpmonitor), whose privacy permissions and root helper
it must never share.

This change is licensed like Wine: LGPL-2.1-or-later.
---
 loader/wine_info.plist.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/loader/wine_info.plist.in
+++ b/loader/wine_info.plist.in
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
     <key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
     <string>wine</string>
     <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
-    <string>org.winehq.wine</string>
+    <string>com.alexparkin.adpmonitor.winehost</string>
     <key>CFBundleInfoDictionaryVersion</key>
     <string>6.0</string>
     <key>CFBundleName</key>
